Purpose: Make corvid:// work: register the corvid scheme, route corvid:// <-> chrome://corvid-<page> and register the Corvid WebUI configs (overlay src-overlay/corvid/webui).
Area: ui
Files: chrome/common/chrome_content_client.cc (kChromeStandardURLSchemes); chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc (BrowserURLHandlerCreated); chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc (RegisterChromeWebUIConfigs); chrome/browser/BUILD.gn, chrome/browser/ui/webui/BUILD.gn (deps on //corvid/webui)
Rebase risk: medium because it adds 1-3 lines to 5 upstream files, all stable registration points; no logic is patched (alias design: docs/notes/corvid-scheme.md)
Origin: original (written for Corvid; the alias-scheme idea, a URL handler pair that maps a brand scheme to chrome://, is also how other forks do it, no third-party patch text reused)

